{
  "name": "screenshot_external_url",
  "description": "Visit an external (non-Modlix) URL in headless Chromium, screenshot at multiple scroll positions and viewport widths, and return a structured Gemini description per shot.\n\nUse for cloning external sites (linear.app, stripe.com, vercel.com) into Modlix. NEVER reach for HTML parsing \u2014 the platform is component-based, not DOM-based; you build Modlix components section-by-section from the structured description.\n\nEach description follows a fixed schema:\n- REGIONS: ordered list of visible page regions with one-sentence layout descriptions\n- COPY: every visible piece of text, region-tagged, verbatim\n- PALETTE: backgrounds, text colors, accent/CTA colors, gradients (hex or named)\n- TYPOGRAPHY: per-region font family/weight/size descriptors\n- ANIMATIONS: visible or implied motion (rotating words, gradient sweeps, scroll-reveals)\n- INTERACTIVE STATES: visible hover/focus styles\n\nWorkflow:\n1. `screenshot_external_url(url=\"https://linear.app\", scroll_positions=[0, 0.5, 1.0])` \u2014 get the structured description.\n2. Build each Modlix section from the REGIONS / COPY / PALETTE / TYPOGRAPHY data \u2014 `add_component` Grid \u2192 child components with the right styles.\n3. For animations, create a global style doc (`create_style`) with `@keyframes` rules and reference the class names from component `styleProperties` \u2014 per-component styleProperties cannot hold `@keyframes`.\n4. After build, `screenshot_page(page_name=<your clone>)` to compare against the source.\n\nThe PNGs are returned in result.data['shots'][i].image_base64 so vision-capable models can also look directly. Text-only models (DeepSeek) should rely on the description text.",
  "input_schema": {
    "type": "object",
    "properties": {
      "url": {
        "type": "string",
        "description": "Absolute URL to clone (must start with http:// or https://)"
      },
      "scroll_positions": {
        "type": "array",
        "description": "Fractions of full scroll height (0.0=top, 1.0=bottom). Default [0, 0.5, 1.0] for top/mid/bottom.",
        "default": [
          0.0,
          0.5,
          1.0
        ],
        "items": {
          "type": "number"
        }
      },
      "viewport_widths": {
        "type": "array",
        "description": "Viewport widths to capture (CSS px). Default [1440]; pass e.g. [1440, 768, 375] for desktop/tablet/mobile.",
        "default": [
          1440
        ],
        "items": {
          "type": "integer"
        }
      },
      "height": {
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "Viewport height in CSS px",
        "default": 900
      },
      "wait_ms": {
        "type": "integer",
        "description": "Milliseconds to wait after page load before first screenshot (lets above-the-fold animations settle)",
        "default": 2500
      }
    },
